      "subject_name": "mge",
      "summary": "`_wofz_rational` selects one of three rational branches with `xp.where` on |z|^2 and Im(z)^2. The value is continuous to ~1e-6 across a seam but the derivative is not, so `jax.grad` of any MGE deflection carries a kink wherever a grid point crosses a boundary. Autodiff derivative error just above the r2=2.5 seam reaches 7.71e-06 relative, against 1.3e-14 for the SciPy path the numpy backend uses.",
